## Slice-once vs leftover concat (Decide card)
| Surface | Span type | Heap now | 7.10 job |
|---------|-----------|----------|----------|
| 7.1 `c_guard_scan_idents` | ident in C-text | **sliced** | do not touch |
| 7.2 `c_sys_exec_last_arg` | last **comma** span | **sliced** | do **not** ident-slice |
| **7.10 `c_parse_secret_env`** | ident after line-start `// SECRET:` | **`name = name + c`** | **I1 apply here** |
| `c_args_strip_cr` | CR **filter** (non-contiguous) | still `out = out + c` | **later 8.6** — not slice-once |
| Lexer `try_scan_ident` | source ident/kw | still `id = id + c2` | **later residual** |
| `c_emit_skip` / `c_emit_struct` / `load_import` / `c_emit_arc` | other name loops | still concat | later hygiene (not 7.10) |
| `c_env_put("__sec__"+name)` | once per directive | one concat | keep |

**Ship-now decision:** slice the **7.10 name span**. Leave filter + lexer + other name loops **named residual**.

